  concept: "Authored objective: Capacitor Charged.\nAuthored requirement: Confirm
    reservoir capacitor voltage reaches 3.1 to 3.7 V in this loaded DC circuit. voltage
    \u2265 3.1 V. voltage \u2264 3.7 V. Connection pair C_RESERVOIR_Positive and
    C_RESERVOIR_Negative.\nGeneral teaching principle: Capacitor voltage and current
    vary with circuit state; transient observations need a stated time and reference.\nOnly
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A storage tank illustrates temporary storage, but electrical capacitance
    has precise circuit equations.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: A transient reading is not automatically a settled reading.
